+Unique `(tenant_id,candidate_id,idempotency_key)` on each ledger gives replay
+identity. Replay requires the same server-derived `actor_id` and request hash;
+same key from a different actor or different semantic request is
+`409 idempotency_conflict`. `succeeded` returns the identical result. A
+`failed_terminal` row never re-drives. `failed_retryable`, or an expired `running`
+row owned by the same actor/request, is reclaimed only by CAS that replaces
+`claim_token`, advances the lease, and increments `attempt_count`. An unexpired
+run returns `202 command_in_progress`. The token must match at closure, so an old
+worker cannot close a reclaimed attempt. The candidate terminal CAS decides
+Add-vs-Dismiss races; one wins and the other receives the stable terminal card.
+Checks require `running` to have token+lease and no completion/result/error;
+`succeeded` to clear token/lease and carry completed time plus the kind-specific
+result; `failed_retryable|failed_terminal` to clear token/lease, carry completed
+time/error, and have no proposal/work/version result. Add success requires both
+proposal and work item; Adjust success requires run/events/version; Dismiss,
+keep, and Restore success forbid all domain-result columns.
 
