+## Native GitHub stack: eight medium PRs
+
+All eight branches may be developed/reviewed as a native dependent stack after B1
+exists; no layer waits for its parent to merge before work begins. Each PR base is
+the previous branch, so GitHub shows only that layer's diff:
+
+| PR | Branch | GitHub base | Scope | Estimate |
+|---|---|---|---|---:|
+| B1 | `codex/meeting-authority-b1-cutover-identity` | `main` | legacy ingest 410/writer kill; provider-subject carrier | 10-14 files; 300-500 LOC |
+| B2 | `codex/meeting-authority-b2-contract-schema` | B1 branch | codecs, exact schema, evidence FKs, projections | 14-20 files; 500-750 LOC |
+| B3 | `codex/meeting-authority-b3-meeting-access` | B2 branch | Python/TS meeting and existing transcript/search authority | 14-20 files; 500-750 LOC |
+| B4 | `codex/meeting-authority-b4-memory-access` | B3 branch | existing memory/knowledge/retrieval caller enforcement only | 12-18 files; 400-650 LOC |
+| B5 | `codex/meeting-authority-b5-work-authority` | B4 branch | proposal/work-item/child/tool authority; atomic transaction seam | 14-20 files; 500-800 LOC |
+| B6 | `codex/meeting-authority-b6-materialize-backfill` | B5 branch | review materialization and post-cutover backfill | 10-16 files; 400-650 LOC |
+| B7 | `codex/meeting-authority-b7-review-commands` | B6 branch | Add/Adjust/Dismiss/Restore services and routes | 14-20 files; 550-850 LOC |
+| B8 | `codex/meeting-authority-b8-web-e2e` | B7 branch | strict web data/card UX and mandatory orchestration | 16-22 files; 550-850 LOC |
+
+Stack protocol is mandatory:
+
+1. Create each branch from its declared parent head and open a draft PR with
+   `Stack position`, parent PR/branch, child PR/branch, parent head SHA, and exact
+   focused validation in the body. GitHub base refs must match the table.
+2. When a lower PR head changes, update descendants bottom-up with
+   `git rebase --onto <new-parent-sha> <old-parent-sha> <child>`; rerun that layer's
+   focused gates, then update its remote ref only with exact old-SHA
+   `--force-with-lease`. Never merge parent content into a child or review a
+   cumulative diff against `main`.
+3. Before review approval, verify each PR's base ref and `merge-base` equals the
+   recorded parent head. A stale child is not reviewable/green.
+4. After a parent merges, rebase the immediate child onto the landed `origin/main`,
+   retarget only that PR to `main`, verify patch identity, then propagate changed
+   parent heads through later descendants. Do not delete a parent branch while a
+   child PR still uses it as base.
+5. CI/check success is per exact layer head. Parent green never substitutes for a
+   child gate, and no stacked branch grants merge authority.
 
